<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Butcher</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 4)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>butcher corpse
</pre>
<p>Cuts a skinned corpse up into meat: legs and arms, steaks (fillets from a 
fish), and scraps, more the bigger the beast. The meat can be eaten, sold 
or cooked (see <a cmd='#'>Help Cook</a>).
</p><p>The corpse must be skinned first (see <a cmd='#'>Help Skin</a>), and you need a dagger 
with you. Corpses of monsters above your own level are harder to butcher. 
If you make a mess of it, all you get is scraps. Butchering is hard work: 
it costs endurance, more for a big carcass, and you can't do it while 
fighting.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Skin</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Cook</a>
</pre>




</div>